<title>CANADA: Thunder Bay cargo up 19 pct April-June 1997 vs '96.</title>
<headline>Thunder Bay cargo up 19 pct April-June 1997 vs '96.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo shipments rose 18.8 percent in the first three months of the 1997 shipping season through the Lake Superior port of Thunder Bay, Thunder Bay Harbour Commission figures to June 24 show.</p>
<p>COMMODITY	    APRIL-JUNE 1997  APRIL-JUNE 1996</p>
<p>Grain		  3,000,638 tonnes 2,350,008 tonnes</p>
<p>Coal		     417,205	    457,351</p>
<p>Potash		   256,589	    280,622</p>
<p>Dry Bulk		  41,420	     98,907</p>
<p>Liquid Bulk	     64,800	     31,199</p>
<p>General Cargo*	  58,364	     14,226</p>
<p>TOTAL:		 3,839,016 tonnes 3,232,313 tonnes</p>
<p>*includes forest products</p>
<p>VESSELS		APRIL-JUNE 1997  APRIL-JUNE 1996</p>
<p>Domestic		 142		  119</p>
<p>Foreign		   42		   27</p>
<p>American		   7		    5</p>
<p>TOTAL:		   191		  151</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
